===Etymology 2===
From {{der|en|frm|sublime}}, from {{der|en|la|sublīmis||high}}, from {{m|la|sub-||up to, upwards}} + a root of uncertain affiliation often identified with {{der|en|la|līmis}}, ablative singular of {{m|la|līmus||oblique}} or {{m|la|līmen||threshold, entrance, lintel}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|er}}

# [[noble|Noble]] and [[majestic]].
#* {{RQ:De Quincey Cicero}}
#*: the '''sublime''' Julian leader
# [[impressive|Impressive]] and [[awe-inspiring]], yet [[simple]].
#: {{ux|en|'''sublime''' scenery}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''sublime''' deed}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1718|authorlink=Matthew Prior|author=Matthew Prior|title=Poems on Several Occasions|chapter=To Dr. Sherlock, On His Practical Discourse Concerning Death|url=https://www.eighteenthcenturypoetry.org/works/pmp18-w0540.shtml|passage=Easy in words thy style, in sense '''sublime'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1839|title=Voices of the Night|author=Henry Wadsworth Longfellow|authorlink=Henry Wadsworth Longfellow|chapter=[[s:The Light of Stars|The Light of Stars]]|passage=Know how '''sublime''' a thing it is / To suffer and be strong.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1897|author=John Munro| title=A Trip to Venus| chapter=VI| chapterurl={{fullurl:s:en:A_Trip_to_Venus/Chapter_VI}}| passage=We had entered the clouds. For half-an-hour we were muffled in a cold, damp mist, and total darkness, and had begun to think of going indoors when, all at once, the car burst into the pure and starlit region of the upper air. A cry of joyous admiration escaped from us all. The spectacle before us was indeed '''sublime'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1993| year_published=1995| author=Richard Klein| isbn=0330340166| publisher=Picador| location=London| title=Cigarettes are sublime| page=62| passage=Cigarettes are poison and they taste bad; they are not exactly beautiful, they are exactly '''sublime'''.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Lifted up; high in place; exalted aloft; uplifted; lofty.
#* {{RQ:Dryden Virgil|Aeneis}}
#*: '''Sublime''' on these a tower of steel is reared.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Elevated by joy; elated.
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Regained|Samson Agonistes|page=96|passage=While thir hearts were jocund and '''ſublime''', / Drunk with Idolatry, drunk with Wine,}}
# Lofty of mien; haughty; proud.
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|book=V|canto=VIII|stanza=30|passage=countenance '''sublime''' and insolent}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=4|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=F08CAAAAQAAJ&pg=PP118|passage=His fair large Front and Eye '''ſublime''' declar'd / Abſolute rule;}}

